---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import PageNav from '../../components/PageNav.astro';
import { t } from '../../i18n';
import type { Locale } from '../../i18n/config';

const locale: Locale = 'en';
---

<DocsLayout>
  <h1>{t(locale, 'nav.sampleIntegrator')}</h1>
  <p class="lead">Run the ticket desk simulator locally to test the full integration flow.</p>

  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>The <code>apps/simulator</code> package is a sample ticket desk that simulates the operator side (CRM/Helpdesk). It demonstrates the complete integration pattern: webhook-driven message reception, E2EE, multi-desk support, and Server-Sent Events for the UI.</p>

  <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Backend running at <code>http://localhost:3000</code></li>
    <li>Web app running at <code>http://localhost:5173</code></li>
    <li>PostgreSQL, Redis running (<code>npm run db:up</code>)</li>
    <li>Migrations applied (<code>npm run db:migrate --workspace=apps/backend</code>)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Running the Simulator</h2>
  <CodeBlock language="bash" code="npm run dev --workspace=apps/simulator" title="Terminal" />

  <p>The simulator runs at <code>http://localhost:4000</code>.</p>

  <h2>Self-Registration</h2>
  <p>The simulator <strong>self-registers</strong> as an integrator on startup. It exposes a callback endpoint at <code>http://localhost:4000/api/integrator-callback</code> that echoes the credentials payload back to SMCI.</p>
  <p>Credentials are persisted to <code>apps/simulator/.keys/integrator.json</code>.</p>

  <h2>Multi-Desk</h2>
  <p>The simulator ships with 10 built-in demo companies (travel, banking, retail, fitness, tech support, etc.). Each desk has its own brand color, icon, and API key. Companies are registered lazily the first time you create a conversation.</p>

  <h2>Webhook-Driven</h2>
  <p>The simulator registers its webhook URL with SMCI and receives events as webhook pushes — it does <strong>not</strong> poll. It relays events to the browser UI over Server-Sent Events (SSE).</p>

  <h2>E2EE</h2>
  <p>Each desk holds its own persistent RSA keypair (stored under <code>apps/simulator/.keys/operators/&lt;handle&gt;/</code>). The simulator encrypts outgoing messages and decrypts incoming ones.</p>

  <h2>Manual Configuration</h2>
  <p>To provide credentials manually instead of self-registering:</p>
  <CodeBlock language="bash" code={`INTEGRATOR_ID=int_xxxxxxxxxxxx
INTEGRATOR_ACCESS_TOKEN=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx`} title="apps/simulator/.env" />

  <h2>Wiping Data</h2>
  <CodeBlock language="bash" code="SIMULATOR_WIPE=true npm run dev --workspace=apps/simulator" title="Terminal" />

  <PageNav
    prev={{ titleKey: 'nav.sdk', path: 'sdk' }}
  />
</DocsLayout>
